EXAMPLES=[{'num':'31','title':'Remove the Product Term','question':'Find the rotation angle removing XY from 9x²+4y²+12xy−x−y=0.','steps':['Identify a=9,b=4 and 2h=12, hence h=6.','The mixed-term condition is −5sin2θ+12cos2θ=0.','Therefore tan2θ=12/5, giving θ=(1/2)tan⁻¹(12/5)≈33.69006753° modulo 90°.','Equivalently tanθ=2/3, so cosθ=3/√13 and sinθ=2/√13.','Substitution gives 13X² − (5/√13)X − (1/√13)Y = 0, with XY coefficient zero.','The source rounds θ to about 34°. Keep the exact angle for substitution; adding 90° swaps the new coordinate directions.'],'answer':'θ=tan⁻¹(2/3)≈33.69006753° modulo 90°.','progressiveSolution':True,'solutionOrigin':'SpaceBook learning enhancement','sourceReferences':[{'page':282,'jpg':'145_page_2.jpg','verification':'Complete source question checked'},{'page':283,'jpg':'146_page_1.jpg','verification':'All angle substitutions and rounding checked'}]}]
